TheThreeLittlePigs.Name: The Three Little Pigs
TheThreeLittlePigs.Blurb: Who's afraid of the big bad wolf?
TheThreeLittlePigs.Summary: A neutral team of three who cannot kill. If all three survive they steal the win; otherwise they win once every killing non-crew is dead.
TheThreeLittlePigs.Team: The Three Little Pigs
TheThreeLittlePigs.Team.Help: When assigned, you team up with two other crewmates as the first, second and third little pig. Teammates are marked ●. If all three are alive when the game ends, you steal the win. If any of you is gone, you win when every killing non-crew is dead.
TheThreeLittlePigs.Team.Short: Survive together
TheThreeLittlePigs.CustomTasks: Use own task counts
TheThreeLittlePigs.CommonTasks: Common tasks
TheThreeLittlePigs.ShortTasks: Short tasks
TheThreeLittlePigs.LongTasks: Long tasks
TheThreeLittlePigs.FirstPercent: First pig: task %
TheThreeLittlePigs.FirstCustomTimer: First pig: custom flash interval
TheThreeLittlePigs.FirstFlashTimer: First pig: flash interval
TheThreeLittlePigs.SecondPercent: Second pig: task %
TheThreeLittlePigs.SecondGuards: Second pig: guards
TheThreeLittlePigs.ThirdPercent: Third pig: task %
TheThreeLittlePigs.ThirdCounters: Third pig: counters
TheFirstLittlePig.Name: First Little Pig
TheFirstLittlePig.Blurb: Even a straw house is better than nothing
TheFirstLittlePig.Summary: The first of the three little pigs. After enough tasks, your screen flashes every kill cooldown.
TheFirstLittlePig.Flash: Straw House
TheFirstLittlePig.Flash.Help: Once you finish the set share of tasks, your screen flashes red at an interval (the kill cooldown by default). If all three pigs are alive at the end, you steal the win.
TheFirstLittlePig.Flash.Short: Flash every kill cooldown
TheSecondLittlePig.Name: Second Little Pig
TheSecondLittlePig.Blurb: A wooden house is reliable, up to a point
TheSecondLittlePig.Summary: The second of the three little pigs. After enough tasks, you can block kills.
TheSecondLittlePig.Guard: Wooden House
TheSecondLittlePig.Guard.Help: Once you finish the set share of tasks, you block kills on you a set number of times. If all three pigs are alive at the end, you steal the win.
TheSecondLittlePig.Guard.Short: Block kills
TheThirdLittlePig.Name: Third Little Pig
TheThirdLittlePig.Blurb: A brick house is as solid as they come
TheThirdLittlePig.Summary: The third of the three little pigs. After enough tasks, you bounce kills back on the killer.
TheThirdLittlePig.Counter: Brick House
TheThirdLittlePig.Counter.Help: Once you finish the set share of tasks, you block kills on you a set number of times and the killer dies. If all three pigs are alive at the end, you steal the win.
TheThirdLittlePig.Counter.Short: Counter kills

# ── フランケンシュタイン (Frankenstein) ──
Frankenstein.Name: Frankenstein
Frankenstein.Blurb: Make a monster out of the dead
Frankenstein.Summary: A neutral who builds monsters from bodies and wins alone after enough monster kills.
Frankenstein.Create: Create Monster
Frankenstein.Create.Help: Use a nearby body to become a monster wearing that person's look. While a monster you can kill with no cooldown; killing drops the body there and returns you to where you started. Monsters cannot be killed: an attack just breaks the monster. A meeting also breaks it. Win alone after the set number of monster kills. You see arrows to bodies.
Frankenstein.Create.Short: Become a monster and kill
Frankenstein.Cooldown: Create cooldown
Frankenstein.WinKillCount: Kills needed to win
Frankenstein.ImpostorVision: Monster has impostor vision
Frankenstein.CanVent: Monster can vent
# ── ユビキタス (Ubiquitous) ──
Ubiquitous.Name: Ubiquitous
Ubiquitous.Blurb: Drones are everywhere
Ubiquitous.Summary: A crewmate who flies a drone to watch and open doors.
Ubiquitous.Call: Call / Return
Ubiquitous.Call.Help: Spawns a drone at your feet. Press again to remove it. When a meeting starts, a flying drone stops where it is and stays for the set number of meetings. People near your stopped drones show on the map.
Ubiquitous.Call.Short: Call a drone
Ubiquitous.Operate: Operate
Ubiquitous.Operate.Help: Pilot the drone. You cannot move while doing so; the camera follows the drone and you can see around it.
Ubiquitous.Operate.Short: Fly the drone
Ubiquitous.DoorHack: Hack Doors
Ubiquitous.DoorHack.Help: While piloting, opens closed doors near the drone.
Ubiquitous.DoorHack.Short: Open nearby doors
Ubiquitous.CallCooldown: Call cooldown
Ubiquitous.OperateCooldown: Operate cooldown
Ubiquitous.LimitOperate: Limit operating time
Ubiquitous.OperateTime: Operating time
Ubiquitous.StayTurns: Meetings a drone stays
Ubiquitous.FlyingSpeed: Drone speed
Ubiquitous.DoorHackCooldown: Door hack cooldown
Ubiquitous.DoorHackScope: Door hack range
Ubiquitous.VisibilityRange: Drone vision range
Ubiquitous.MapShowColor: Show colors on the map
# ── バランサー (Balancer) ──
Balancer.Name: Balancer
Balancer.Blurb: Put them on the scales
Balancer.Summary: A crewmate who puts two people on the scales in a meeting so one of them must go.
Balancer.Balance: Balance
Balancer.Balance.Help: Pick two people in a meeting to put them on the scales. Everyone else's card and skip disappear and everyone votes again for one of the two (within the set time). The one with more votes is ejected; on a tie both are ejected. If one dies meanwhile, the other is ejected.
Balancer.Balance.Short: Eject one of two
Balancer.VoteTime: Balance voting time
Balancer.UseCount: Uses
Balancer.RandomVote: Non-voters vote at random
Balancer.Started: The scales tip... vote for one of them
Balancer.Title.Either: Choose one
Balancer.Title.Average: Which one goes?
Balancer.Title.YouVote: You decide
Balancer.Title.EitherExile: One of them will be ejected
Balancer.Title.WhoIsImpostor: Who is the impostor?
Balancer.Title.GetBalance: Will the scales balance?
Balancer.Title.PleaseVote: Vote
Balancer.DoubleExile: The scales balanced. Both were ejected
Balancer.OnePlayerDead: One fell, so the other was ejected
Balancer.NoPlayer: No one is left on the scales

